Chapter I: THE INSOLVENCY AND BANKRUPTCY BOARD OF INDIA | Section 190: Removal of member from office**

**190. Removal of member from office** .—The Central Government may remove a member from office if he—

( _a_ ) is an undischarged bankrupt as defined under Part III;

( _b_ ) has become physically or mentally incapable of acting as a member;

( _c_ ) has been convicted of an offence, which in the opinion of the Central Government involves moral turpitude;

( _d_ ) has, so abused his position as to render his continuation in office detrimental to the public interest:

Provided that no member shall be removed under clause ( _d_ ) unless he has been given a reasonable opportunity of being heard in the matter.

